\section*{Complex group-ring traces vanish on infinite-order classes}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. The Bass trace restriction is claimed for complex group rings of arbitrary discrete groups, implying triviality of scalar idempotents for torsion-free groups over characteristic-zero domains.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} For an arbitrary discrete group \(G\), let \(\operatorname{HS}_G\) be the Hattori--Stallings trace, whose value at a conjugacy class sums the coefficients on that class. For every \(x\in K_0(\mathbb C[G])\),
\[
 |g|=\infty\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\operatorname{HS}_G(x)([g])=0.
\]
The torsion-free corollary states that, for every \(q\ge1\) and idempotent \(e\in M_q(\mathbb C[G])\), its identity-coefficient trace equals the rank of its augmentation matrix:
\[
 \tau_{G,q}(e)=\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb C}(\epsilon_{G,q}(e)).
\]
For such \(G\), any commutative unital domain \(R\) of characteristic zero satisfies
\[
 e\in R[G],\ e^2=e\quad\Longrightarrow\quad e\in\{0,1\}.
\]
The characteristic-zero qualification does not cover positive-characteristic group rings.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
An idempotent is encoded by finite cyclic path configurations whose weighted deletion relations generate cycles. Exterior differential forms and a cyclic Pfaffian identity detect forbidden conjugacy support; trace-rank arguments then turn the complex trace conclusion into the stated idempotent consequence.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The main theorem makes the Hattori--Stallings trace of every K\_0(C G) class vanish on each infinite-order conjugacy class. An idempotent matrix represents a projective class, and its trace is the displayed sum of diagonal coefficients. lean/docs/207.md covers this exact complex trace conclusion. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 207, the documented Lean statements give complex group-ring Bass trace support and characteristic-zero torsion-free trace rank and idempotent triviality. The separate $\ell^1$ theorem is not selected. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{BassTorsionFree.lean}, \texttt{BassTrace.lean}. Named declarations include \texttt{OAI.BassTrace.RightProjective.bassTraceModules\_vanishing\_and\_support}. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

